3. Dependencies with licenses other than MIT/ISC/BSD/Apache-2.0
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The app (root package.json), installed from the npm registry:
- xlsx 0.18.5 (SheetJS Community Edition): Apache-2.0. Known vulnerabilities, see README.
- web-push 3.6.7: MPL-2.0. Loaded at runtime by the edge function send-web-push (npm: specifier), not bundled in
  this repository.
- axe-core: MPL-2.0. Development dependency only (accessibility lint rules), not shipped in the front end build.

The QR service (qr-service/package.json), summary; the details are in qr-service/NOTICE:
- libsignal 6.0.0: GPL-3.0, a dependency of Baileys. The source code in qr-service/ only declares the
  dependency; a container image that includes node_modules is a combined work that includes GPL-3.0 code, and
  whoever distributes such an image must comply with the GPL-3.0 for that component.
- codec-parser: LGPL-3.0-or-later, through audio-decode. Used unmodified, as a separate module.
- @img/sharp-libvips-*: LGPL-3.0-or-later, prebuilt binaries used by sharp. Used unmodified, dynamically linked.

The full list of licenses of the installed packages can be produced with `npx license-checker --summary`, run at
the root and inside qr-service/ (or by reading the "license" fields of each package-lock.json).

